<!--
  libsofia_sip_ua.dll - the sofia-sip DLL the NVP DSP links (ENG-268).

  Replaces the prebuilt static libsofia_sip_ua_static.lib of unknown provenance.
  Upstream ships libsofia_sip_ua.vcproj here, but it is VS2005 (Version="8.00") and
  modern VS no longer upgrades .vcproj - hence a new project rather than an upgrade.

  The SOURCE LIST is FreeSWITCH's (libs/win32/sofia/libsofia_sip_ua_static.2017.vcxproj
  in Noetica/nvp_freeswitch), NOT upstream's DLL project. Upstream's omits tport_tls.c,
  tport_type_tls.c, tport_type_ws.c, ws.c and su_string.c - so it would silently drop TLS,
  which the DSP registers over. FreeSWITCH's list is what built the library we ship.

  EXPORTS are macro-driven: IN_LIBSOFIA_SIP_UA and IN_LIBSOFIA_SRES make SOFIAPUBFUN and
  SRESPUBFUN expand to __declspec(dllexport) (su_config.h, sres_config.h). The
  LIBSOFIA_SIP_UA_STATIC / LIBSRES_STATIC defines the static build uses must NOT be set
  here - they suppress those macros entirely. Note the failure is SILENT, not a link
  error: the DLL still builds, but exports collapse to only the ~618 symbols the twelve
  generated *_tag_ref.c files dllexport themselves. The CI export-count check is what
  catches that, so do not weaken it.

  Upstream's sofia-sip-ua.def is deliberately NOT used, though it looks like the safer
  declarative option. It is stale and over-broad for this source set: linking against it
  gave 32 unresolved externals. Some of those symbols no longer exist anywhere in 1.13.14
  (auth_mod_check_ireq); others live in files FreeSWITCH excludes (nta_msg_send and
  nta_leg_stateful, in nta_compat.c). Checked against the artifact we actually ship: none
  of the 32 are in libsofia_sip_ua_static.lib either, so the 171-file list is right and
  the .def is wrong for it. It would also double-export the *_tag_ref.c symbols, which
  carry their own __declspec(dllexport) (LNK4197).

  17 of the sources are GENERATED (sip_tag.c, msg_mime_table.c, http_tag.c, twelve
  *_tag_ref.c, ...), and sofia_features.h + win32\config.h are generated too. Run BOTH
  win32\build_sources.cmd and win32\version_files.cmd before building, from a checkout
  with LF line endings - the awk splits templates on form-feed+LF and silently emits
  empty output on a CRLF checkout. version_files.cmd is what writes win32\config.h;
  without it every sdp/soa/tport source fails C1083 on config.h.

  Dependencies come from pinned Noetica mirrors, overridable for CI:
    PthreadsDir  - Noetica/pthreads-win32  (pthread.h; sofia sets SU_HAVE_PTHREADS 1)
    OpenSslDir   - Noetica/openssl-win64   (headers + static libs for tport_tls.c)
  The OpenSSL libs are /MT built with /Zl, so they carry no CRT directive and link into
  this /MD DLL. Do not "correct" that apparent mismatch; treat LNK4098 as a real finding.
-->
